('AI-001','2026-05-07','Global','Technological','Agentic AI','Cross-sector','Trend','Act','Enterprise AI agents move from demos to workflow orchestration','Gartner’s updated agentic-AI outlook says task-specific AI agents are moving into enterprise applications and workflow orchestration, with a projected 40% of enterprise apps including such agents by the end of 2026. The opportunity is faster innovation workflows; the risk is weak governance, unclear accountability and brittle automation as agents coordinate work across tools and teams.','OpenAI; Google DeepMind; Anthropic; Microsoft; Salesforce; enterprise software vendors; research organisations','Mixed','Share of enterprise applications with task-specific AI agents; agent-to-agent protocols; enterprise spending; failed or cancelled agent projects; workflow-orchestration use cases',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts: agents can continuously monitor signals and synthesise options, but governance and auditability are needed to avoid automated false positives and accountability gaps during validation.','https://www.gartner.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2025-08-26-gartner-predicts-40-percent-of-enterprise-apps-will-feature-task-specific-ai-agents-by-2026-up-from-less-than-5-percent-in-2025','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-002','2026-05-10','Global','Technological','AI for science','Education/research','Trend','Prepare','AI for science advances while reproducibility remains the validation bottleneck','The 2026 AI Index reports rapid growth in AI-related scientific output, domain foundation models and end-to-end research agents, but also large gaps in replication and code reliability. The signal is that AI can accelerate hypothesis generation, while innovation teams must strengthen reproducibility and experimental validation before scaling R&D decisions.','Stanford HAI; AI labs; universities; research funders; scientific publishers; R&D organisations','Mixed','AI-related scientific publications; AI foundation models for science; replication benchmark scores; code failure rates; validated AI co-scientist cases',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts','Develop solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts; Develop solutions: AI can widen scientific opportunity scouting, but validation gates must check reproducibility, experimental transferability and code reliability before development.','https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report/science','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-003','2026-05-07','EU / Global','Political','AI regulation','Cross-sector','Emerging issue','Act','AI Act compliance becomes a design constraint for innovation portfolios','The EU AI Act and related GPAI rules make regulatory classification, documentation, risk management and post-market monitoring more central to AI-enabled innovation. The 2026 implementation picture is now more nuanced because the Commission’s simplification package and political agreement adjust some high-risk timelines while preserving core obligations, making compliance timing and standards readiness part of innovation planning.','European Commission; national market surveillance authorities; AI model providers; enterprise adopters','Mixed','Compliance budgets; number of high-risk AI use cases; conformity-assessment activity; GPAI documentation practices; harmonised standards readiness; AI Act implementation milestones',array['Identify opportunities','Create concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Create concepts; Deploy solutions: regulatory classification, standards readiness and documentation needs should shape opportunity framing, concept criteria and launch readiness for AI-enabled offerings.','https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/regulatory-framework-ai','Regulatory document','excel-database'),
('AI-004','2026-05-10','Global','Economic','AI infrastructure','ICT/software','Trend','Prepare','Compute concentration shapes who can innovate with frontier AI','The 2026 AI Index highlights rapid growth in global AI compute capacity, private investment and frontier-model infrastructure, while access remains concentrated among large firms and regions with chips, data centres and capital. This may concentrate frontier experimentation while increasing demand for efficient models and shared compute.','Stanford HAI; Epoch AI; NVIDIA; cloud hyperscalers; national AI infrastructure initiatives; start-ups','Mixed','AI compute capacity; GPU availability; AI private investment; cloud AI pricing; national compute programmes',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts: compute concentration affects which opportunities are feasible and which concepts can be validated at realistic scale.','https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-005','2026-05-10','Global','Environmental','AI infrastructure','Energy','Emerging issue','Act','AI data-centre energy and water footprint enters innovation governance','IEA’s 2026 analysis shows data-centre electricity demand grew sharply in 2025, with AI-focused data centres growing faster and energy-intensive AI use cases such as video, reasoning and agents emerging. Innovation teams may face stronger disclosure, siting, water and energy-efficiency requirements for AI-enabled offerings.','IEA; hyperscalers; data-centre operators; utilities; regulators; municipalities; sustainability teams','Mixed','Data-centre electricity demand; AI-focused data-centre growth; water-use disclosures; grid-connection queues; AI workload energy intensity',array['Identify opportunities','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Deploy solutions: AI roadmaps need sustainability criteria early, and scaling decisions should account for energy, water and grid constraints.','https://www.iea.org/reports/key-questions-on-energy-and-ai/executive-summary','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-006','2026-05-07','Global','Technological','AI-ready data','Cross-sector','Trend','Act','AI-ready data becomes a prerequisite for scalable innovation','Gartner’s 2026 data-and-analytics predictions reinforce that scalable AI depends on governed context, semantic layers and machine-verifiable data contracts rather than isolated models alone. This shifts innovation management toward data-product thinking, reusable knowledge assets, governed context layers and evaluation-ready data foundations.','Gartner; data platform vendors; chief data officers; AI governance teams; innovation teams','Opportunity','Data-product initiatives; metadata quality; semantic-layer investments; context graphs; retrieval-augmented generation deployments; enterprise knowledge graphs; data contracts',array['Identify opportunities','Create concepts','Validate concepts']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Create concepts; Validate concepts: AI-ready data and context infrastructure improve signal retrieval, idea reuse and evidence quality during validation.','https://www.gartner.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2026-03-11-gartner-announces-top-predictions-for-data-and-analytics-in-2026','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-007','2026-05-07','Global','Technological','Small language models / edge AI','Manufacturing','Trend','Prepare','Small and specialised models make AI deployable closer to products and factories','Recent edge-AI analysis points to a shift from cloud-centric AI toward distributed inference on devices, machines and infrastructure. Smaller, domain-tuned and on-device AI models can reduce latency, cost, privacy and connectivity barriers, enabling embedded innovation in products, industrial systems and field services where cloud-only AI is unsuitable.','Model developers; semiconductor firms; industrial automation vendors; edge-AI platform providers; product companies','Opportunity','On-device model releases; edge AI chip shipments; industrial pilots; inference cost reductions; edge orchestration platforms; privacy-driven local AI deployments',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts','Develop solutions','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts; Develop solutions; Deploy solutions: edge AI changes concept options and enables realistic field validation, product development and deployment under latency, cost, connectivity and privacy constraints.','https://www.mapegy.com/reports/edge-ai-technology-report','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-008','2026-05-10','Global','Technological','Synthetic data','Healthcare/life sciences','Emerging issue','Prepare','Synthetic health data shifts from privacy workaround to validated infrastructure','The EU-backed SYNTHIA initiative is developing validated synthetic-data generation methods for healthcare AI across clinical, genomic, imaging and mobile-health data. Synthetic data can support privacy-preserving innovation, but evidence quality, realism and transferability remain central validation questions.','SYNTHIA consortium; Innovative Health Initiative; NICE; healthcare AI firms; clinical researchers; regulators','Mixed','Synthetic-data validation frameworks; healthcare synthetic-data pilots; regulatory acceptance; model performance on real-world data',array['Validate concepts','Develop solutions']::text[],'Validate concepts; Develop solutions: synthetic data can expand test coverage, but teams must document realism, bias and transferability before relying on it in developed solutions.','https://www.ihi-synthia.eu/','Case example','excel-database'),
('AI-009','2026-05-10','Global','Cultural','Generative AI','Creative industries/media','Emerging issue','Act','AI-generated content disclosure becomes operational trust infrastructure','The European Commission’s AI Office is developing a Code of Practice for marking and labelling AI-generated content to support Article 50 transparency obligations. AI-content marking, deepfake labelling and provenance are becoming engineering and governance tasks, reducing ambiguity for users while increasing operational obligations for market research, media, product and communication workflows.','European Commission; AI Office; content platforms; brands; publishers; provenance standards bodies; generative AI providers and deployers','Mixed','AI labels; C2PA/content-credential adoption; deepfake disclosure rules; detection tools; platform policy updates; Article 50 guidance and code milestones',array['Identify opportunities','Create concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Create concepts; Deploy solutions: insight protocols and market-facing content need provenance, labelling and disclosure checks before concepts are scaled.','https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/code-practice-ai-generated-content','Standard/guideline','excel-database'),
('AI-010','2026-05-10','Global','Political','AI IP/content rights','Legal/professional services','Emerging issue','Act','Copyright and training-data transparency move into AI product due diligence','The UK Government’s 2026 copyright and AI report emphasizes evidence-building, training-data transparency, licensing markets and technical standards rather than a broad exception. GenAI-enabled innovation may need stronger IP provenance and licensing documentation before concepts enter commercial use.','UK Government; AI developers; publishers; creators; enterprise legal teams; IP offices; procurement teams','Risk','Training-data disclosures; licensing deals; opt-out tools; copyright litigation outcomes; enterprise AI indemnity terms',array['Create concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Deploy solutions: AI-assisted concepts need IP provenance checks before they enter formal development and commercial use.','https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/report-and-impact-assessment-on-copyright-and-artificial-intelligence/report-on-copyright-and-artificial-intelligence','Regulatory document','excel-database'),
('AI-011','2026-05-10','Global','Social','AI skills/workforce','Education/research','Trend','Act','AI shifts innovation work toward judgement, orchestration and evaluation skills','Deloitte’s 2026 enterprise AI research shows that organisations are expanding access and AI fluency, while fewer are redesigning jobs and workflows. Innovation teams need judgement, orchestration, validation and governance skills rather than only tool-use familiarity.','Deloitte; employers; HR teams; universities; professional associations; AI tool vendors; innovation teams','Mixed','AI fluency programmes; job redesign initiatives; agent-orchestration training; job postings mentioning AI; workflow transformation metrics',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts: innovation capability-building should improve AI literacy, task design and validation competence for human-AI collaboration.','https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/what-we-do/capabilities/applied-artificial-intelligence/content/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-012','2026-05-10','Global','Technological','AI robotics/autonomous labs','Pharma/biotech','Weak signal','Watch','Self-driving labs move toward scientific infrastructure but validation gaps remain','The 2026 AI Index reports that AI is increasingly embedded in scientific pipelines and that AI agents can support end-to-end research tasks, though performance still trails expert baselines and reproducibility remains difficult. Autonomous labs may accelerate R&D where robotics, data quality and human validation are integrated.','Stanford HAI; AI labs; academic labs; pharma firms; materials companies; robotics vendors; research funders','Opportunity','Autonomous-lab publications; AI co-scientist cases; closed-loop experiment cycles; robotic lab investments; replication evidence',array['Validate concepts','Develop solutions']::text[],'Validate concepts; Develop solutions: self-driving labs can compress design-build-test-learn cycles if validation evidence and physical integration are strong.','https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report/science','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-013','2026-05-10','Global','Economic','Generative AI','Cross-sector','Trend','Act','GenAI productivity gains depend on workflow redesign, not tool access','Deloitte’s 2026 enterprise AI report shows worker access and production use expanding, but only a minority of organisations are deeply transforming processes or jobs around AI. Value capture increasingly depends on redesigned workflows, governance and complementary capabilities.','Deloitte; enterprises; consultancies; universities; AI vendors; productivity researchers','Mixed','AI projects in production; workflow redesign cases; productivity metrics; AI ROI reporting; role redesign initiatives',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts; Deploy solutions: AI productivity gains depend on redesigned workflows, validated use cases and disciplined scaling rather than tool access alone.','https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/what-we-do/capabilities/applied-artificial-intelligence/content/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-014','2026-05-10','Global','Political','AI governance','Public sector','Trend','Prepare','AI sovereignty becomes central to national innovation investment','The 2026 AI Index shows national AI strategies expanding and AI sovereignty becoming a central policy principle, while public compute and infrastructure remain unevenly distributed. Public-private innovation opportunities may grow, but standards, procurement and data access may fragment.','Stanford HAI; national governments; public research funders; OECD countries; EU; regional alliances','Mixed','National AI strategies; sovereign compute clusters; public AI funding; data localisation measures; public procurement rules',array['Identify opportunities']::text[],'Identify opportunities: national AI strategies, funding priorities and sovereignty requirements should shape opportunity framing and ecosystem positioning.','https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report/policy-and-governance','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-015','2026-05-10','Global South','Economic','Responsible AI','Public sector','Trend','Prepare','Inclusive AI agenda links innovation policy to local capability and development outcomes','Recent Global South AI commentary highlights local languages, indigenous knowledge, digital public infrastructure and shared compute as priorities for more inclusive AI. This creates opportunities for frugal, contextual and public-value innovation, while challenging imported one-size-fits-all AI models.','World Economic Forum; Global South governments; local AI communities; development banks; universities; civil society','Opportunity','Local-language model releases; public compute programmes; AI readiness indices; DPI-linked AI services; inclusion metrics',array['Identify opportunities']::text[],'Identify opportunities: inclusion, infrastructure and local capability gaps should be treated as opportunity-framing criteria for AI-enabled public-value innovation.','https://www.weforum.org/stories/2026/02/how-the-global-south-is-reimagining-the-future-of-ai/','Expert assessment','excel-database'),
('AI-016','2026-05-10','Global','Technological','AI safety & assurance','Cross-sector','Emerging issue','Act','AI evaluation and assurance become core innovation gates','McKinsey’s 2026 AI trust research highlights that governance and active risk mitigation are lagging behind the shift to agentic AI. Evaluation, red-teaming, monitoring and incident response are becoming core innovation controls for systems with autonomy or high impact.','McKinsey; AI Safety Institutes; model providers; auditors; enterprise risk teams; standards bodies','Mixed','Responsible AI maturity scores; safety evaluation frameworks; third-party audits; AI incidents; agent control failures',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts','Develop solutions','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts; Develop solutions; Deploy solutions: AI assurance adds evaluation criteria to concepts, validation gates and deployment readiness.','https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/tech-and-ai/our-insights/tech-forward/state-of-ai-trust-in-2026-shifting-to-the-agentic-era','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-017','2026-05-10','Global','Technological','Multimodal AI','Consumer goods','Trend','Prepare','Multimodal AI changes market sensing while exposing task-specific failure modes','Coverage of the 2026 AI Index notes that multimodal models are conquering many benchmarks but still fail at basic visual tasks such as reading clocks. This expands insight and prototyping possibilities while reinforcing the need for realistic user-context validation.','Stanford HAI; IEEE Spectrum; AI labs; design software vendors; market research firms; consumer brands','Mixed','Multimodal model releases; benchmark performance gaps; user-context tests; design-tool integrations; multimodal failure cases',array['Identify opportunities','Create concepts']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Create concepts: multimodal AI expands market sensing and concept generation, while realistic user validation remains necessary.','https://spectrum.ieee.org/state-of-ai-index-2026','News/press release','excel-database'),
('AI-018','2026-05-10','Global','Technological','Open-weight models','ICT/software','Trend','Prepare','Open-weight and open-source AI expand experimentation but shift governance to adopters','The 2026 AI Index reports rapid growth in AI-related open-source activity and broader participation in AI development. Open-weight and permissively licensed models lower experimentation barriers but place more responsibility for security, testing and compliance on adopters.','Stanford HAI; Meta; Mistral AI; Hugging Face; open-source communities; enterprises','Mixed','Open model downloads; GitHub AI projects; fine-tuning activity; local deployments; misuse incidents',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts','Develop solutions','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts; Develop solutions; Deploy solutions: open-weight models enable rapid experimentation, but local governance is needed before deployment.','https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-019','2026-05-10','Global','Cultural','Generative AI','Education/research','Trend','Act','Research AI-use disclosure becomes part of integrity governance','The European Commission’s May 2026 living guidelines for generative AI in research emphasize researcher responsibility, disclosure, privacy, IP protection, reproducibility and limits on AI use in sensitive evaluation activities. AI-assisted science can increase productivity but requires clearer integrity routines.','European Commission; ERA Forum; universities; research funders; publishers; researchers; innovation teams','Mixed','AI-use disclosure policies; research-integrity guidelines; peer-review AI restrictions; reproducibility documentation; AI-assisted publication cases',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts: AI-assisted research requires explicit norms for evidence quality, reproducibility and accountability during scouting and validation.','https://research-and-innovation.ec.europa.eu/document/download/2b6cf7e5-36ac-41cb-aab5-0d32050143dc_en?filename=ec_rtd_ai-guidelines.pdf','Standard/guideline','excel-database'),
('AI-020','2026-05-10','Global','Technological','AI-enabled cyber/security','Defence/security','Emerging issue','Act','AI accelerates cyber-enabled fraud and attacks on innovation assets','The WEF Global Cybersecurity Outlook 2026 identifies AI adoption, AI-related vulnerabilities, cyber-enabled fraud and geopolitical fragmentation as major cyber-risk drivers. Innovation portfolios involving AI, IP and partners may face higher fraud, deepfake, phishing and supply-chain exposure.','World Economic Forum; Accenture; CISOs; threat actors; cybersecurity firms; enterprises; governments','Risk','AI-enabled phishing; deepfake fraud; cyber-enabled payment fraud; AI security reviews; supply-chain cyber incidents',array['Validate concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Validate concepts; Deploy solutions: AI-enabled security risk should be tested before scaling innovation assets and partner-facing deployments.','https://www.weforum.org/publications/global-cybersecurity-outlook-2026/','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-021','2026-05-07','EU / Global','Political','AI regulation','Cross-sector','Emerging issue','Prepare','AI Act simplification proposals make compliance timing a moving target','The EU Digital Omnibus proposal would adjust high-risk AI timelines, sandboxing and documentation obligations. Innovation teams may gain flexibility, but must manage uncertainty around standards readiness, market surveillance and launch timing.','European Commission; AI Office; national market surveillance authorities; enterprise AI providers; product manufacturers','Mixed','AI Act implementation milestones; harmonised standards readiness; regulatory sandbox participation; compliance roadmap changes',array['Identify opportunities','Create concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Create concepts; Deploy solutions: regulatory timing assumptions should be revisited from opportunity framing through concept criteria and launch commitments.','https://www.cooley.com/news/insight/2025/2025-11-24-eu-ai-act-proposed-digital-omnibus-on-ai-will-impact-businesses-ai-compliance-roadmaps','Regulatory document','excel-database'),
('AI-022','2026-05-07','Global','Environmental','AI infrastructure','Energy','Emerging issue','Prepare','AI data-centre footprint becomes an infrastructure governance issue','Recent AI Index reporting highlights rising model training emissions, data-centre power capacity and inference-related water use. The signal is less about model capability than about how innovation portfolios account for energy, water and local infrastructure constraints.','Stanford HAI; hyperscalers; utilities; energy regulators; municipalities; sustainability teams','Mixed','AI data-centre power capacity; model training emissions; inference water-use estimates; local permitting disputes',array['Identify opportunities','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Deploy solutions: resource intensity should be screened early and reflected in scaling assumptions for AI-enabled offerings.','https://hai.stanford.edu/news/inside-the-ai-index-12-takeaways-from-the-2026-report','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-023','2026-05-07','Global South / Global','Social','AI skills/workforce','Education/research','Emerging issue','Act','GenAI labour-market disruption may arrive before productivity dividends','ILO and World Bank research indicates that digital divides and task differences may cause developing economies to experience displacement or disruption before they can capture GenAI productivity gains. This raises inclusion and reskilling questions for innovation systems.','ILO; World Bank; employers; workers; training providers; governments; innovation teams','Risk','GenAI exposure by occupation; internet access gaps; reskilling programme uptake; automation of clerical and administrative roles',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts: inclusive AI adoption requires opportunity framing and validation that account for skills, access and labour-market transition risks.','https://www.ilo.org/resource/news/new-ilo%E2%80%93world-bank-paper-highlights-uneven-global-impact-generative-ai-jobs','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-024','2026-05-07','UK / Global','Cultural','AI IP/content rights','Creative industries/media','Discontinuity','Prepare','Copyright policy shifts toward transparency and licensing over broad AI exceptions','The UK government’s 2026 copyright and AI report moves away from a broad opt-out exception and emphasises evidence-building, transparency, technical standards and licensing. This may reshape how AI-enabled creative and research workflows source data.','UK Government; creators; publishers; AI developers; collective management organisations; creative industries','Mixed','AI training transparency rules; licensing deals; creator opt-out tools; copyright litigation outcomes',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts; Deploy solutions: GenAI-enabled creative workflows need licensing and transparency assumptions tested before deployment.','https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/report-and-impact-assessment-on-copyright-and-artificial-intelligence/report-on-copyright-and-artificial-intelligence','Regulatory document','excel-database'),
('AI-025','2026-05-07','Global','Political','AI governance','Public sector','Trend','Prepare','AI sovereignty becomes a central frame for national innovation investment','The 2026 AI Index notes rapid expansion of national AI strategies and growing emphasis on AI sovereignty, while infrastructure is unevenly distributed across regions. This creates opportunities for public-private innovation but may also fragment standards and data access.','National governments; Stanford HAI; public research funders; AI infrastructure providers; regional alliances','Opportunity','National AI strategies; state-backed AI compute clusters; data localisation measures; public AI funding commitments',array['Identify opportunities']::text[],'Identify opportunities: AI sovereignty, public funding and data governance requirements should shape opportunity selection and ecosystem positioning.','https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report/policy-and-governance','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-026','2026-05-06','Global','Political','AI public governance','Public sector','Emerging issue','Prepare','UN Global Dialogue turns AI governance into a multilateral coordination test','The UN Global Dialogue on AI Governance is moving from mandate to consultation, creating a forum for states, firms, civil society and scientists to align AI rules, risk evaluation and capacity-building. The opportunity is more coherent global governance; the risk is slow consensus or lowest-common-denominator commitments.','United Nations; ITU; member states; AI firms; civil society; scientific panel; public-sector innovators','Mixed','UN consultation milestones; roadmap drafts; participation from Global South actors; references to AI governance in national strategies',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts: multilateral governance norms should inform opportunity framing and the validation of partnership, procurement and risk assumptions.','https://www.un.org/global-dialogue-ai-governance/en/consultations','Regulatory document','excel-database'),
('AI-027','2026-05-06','Global / US','Social','AI public opinion/trust','Cross-sector','Emerging issue','Act','Expert-public trust gap becomes a barrier to AI-enabled innovation','The 2026 AI Index shows rising AI optimism alongside anxiety, with large gaps between experts and the public on jobs, the economy and medical care. Social acceptance may become a gating factor for innovation even where technical feasibility is strong.','Stanford HAI; Pew Research Center; Gallup; employers; consumers; regulators; innovation teams','Risk','AI trust surveys; public nervousness indicators; employee adoption sentiment; customer opt-out or complaint rates',array['Identify opportunities','Create concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Create concepts; Deploy solutions: trust, explainability and perceived fairness should be considered during sensing, concept design and scaling decisions.','https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report/public-opinion','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-028','2026-05-06','Global','Economic','AI workforce redesign','Cross-sector','Trend','Act','AI value capture shifts from tool access to job and workflow redesign','Deloitte’s 2026 enterprise AI research indicates that many organisations are expanding worker access and AI fluency, but fewer are redesigning roles, workflows and operating models. Innovation advantage may shift to firms that redesign work rather than merely deploy tools.','Deloitte; enterprise leaders; HR teams; innovation managers; workers; AI vendors','Opportunity','Share of AI projects in production; job redesign initiatives; AI fluency programmes; workflow transformation metrics',array['Identify opportunities','Create concepts','Validate concepts','Develop solutions','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Create concepts; Validate concepts; Develop solutions; Deploy solutions: workflow redesign affects the full ISO innovation process from opportunity framing to scaled deployment.','https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/what-we-do/capabilities/applied-artificial-intelligence/content/state-of-ai-in-the-enterprise.html','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-029','2026-05-29','US / Global','Political','AI compliance','Legal/professional services','Trend','Act','State-level AI law patchwork increases compliance drag on AI innovation','Current 2026 state-level AI and chatbot trackers show a fast-expanding U.S. patchwork across high-risk systems, companion chatbots, minors, disclosures, safety protocols and professional-service restrictions. Multi-jurisdiction innovation teams may face higher compliance costs, more product variants and slower scaling decisions unless governance is designed for state-by-state divergence.','US state legislatures; attorneys general; compliance teams; employers; AI developers; legal counsel','Risk','Number of state AI bills; chatbot-specific bills; effective dates; impact-assessment requirements; bias-audit mandates; disclosure and safety requirements',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts; Deploy solutions: jurisdictional compliance requirements should shape concepts, risk validation and launch decisions.','https://fpf.org/2026-chatbot-legislation-tracker/','Legal analysis','excel-database'),
('AI-030','2026-05-06','Global','Environmental','AI energy governance','Energy','Discontinuity','Act','AI infrastructure forces energy strategy into innovation portfolio decisions','Recent energy-focused analysis highlights that data-centre electricity demand, power density, grid constraints and cooling requirements are becoming strategic constraints for AI scaling. This creates opportunities for efficiency and energy partnerships, while raising cost, siting and sustainability risks.','IEA; data-centre operators; cloud hyperscalers; utilities; energy regulators; sustainability teams; innovation leaders','Mixed','Data-centre electricity demand; rack power density; grid connection delays; cooling technology adoption; AI workload energy disclosures',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts; Deploy solutions: energy architecture and workload efficiency should be tested early and embedded in scale-up decisions.','https://www.sardinasystems.com/news/ais-electricity-problem-or-what-the-latest-data-actually-shows/','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-031','2026-05-29','EU / Local','Political','AI public governance','Public sector','Weak signal','Watch','Public-sector algorithm transparency becomes a reusable governance pattern','OECD.AI’s 2026 coverage of the UK Algorithmic Transparency Recording Standard highlights how practical registers, templates and reporting standards are becoming reusable accountability mechanisms for government AI. Local AI registries remain uneven, but standardised transparency records may spread procurement and legitimacy expectations for public innovation pilots.','OECD.AI; UK public authorities; city governments; civic tech groups; procurement teams; residents','Mixed','Algorithmic transparency standards; public AI registers; procurement clauses requiring AI disclosure; civic requests for algorithm transparency; published transparency records',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts: local transparency expectations may shape which public-sector AI ideas are legitimate and what evidence is needed before pilots proceed.','https://oecd.ai/','Policy brief','excel-database'),
('AI-033','2026-05-10','Global South / Local','Social','AI skills/workforce','Education/research','Weak signal','Watch','Non-formal AI skills pathways broaden innovation capability signals','The 2026 AI Index education chapter reports that people are acquiring AI skills outside formal education and advertising AI skills on resumes, while formal AI education is slower to scale in many countries. This may make micro-credentials and practical AI portfolios more relevant to innovation capability-building.','Stanford HAI; learners; employers; online training platforms; universities; community organisations; public innovation hubs','Opportunity','AI skills on resumes; micro-credentials; AI literacy growth; employer recognition of non-formal AI credentials',array['Identify opportunities']::text[],'Identify opportunities: alternative AI capability signals may broaden who can participate in innovation scouting and early-stage experimentation.','https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report/education','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-034','2026-05-10','Japan / Global','Cultural','AI public opinion/trust','Consumer goods','Weak signal','Watch','Human-made and low-AI authenticity claims gain support from copyright transparency debates','The UK’s 2026 copyright and AI report highlights transparency, labelling, human creativity and digital replica risks. Niche consumer and creative segments may increasingly value visible human authorship or constrained AI use as part of authenticity and trust.','UK Government; craft brands; luxury marketers; artists; design studios; consumer communities; copyright offices','Mixed','Human-made product claims; AI-use labels; creator opt-out tools; premium pricing for non-AI creative processes; consumer sentiment',array['Create concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Deploy solutions: concept narratives and launch strategies may need to account for demand for visible human authorship or limited AI involvement.','https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/report-and-impact-assessment-on-copyright-and-artificial-intelligence/report-on-copyright-and-artificial-intelligence','Regulatory document','excel-database'),
('AI-035','2026-05-10','Nordics / Local','Environmental','AI energy governance','Energy','Weak signal','Watch','AI data-centre waste heat becomes a circular infrastructure design option','European Commission coverage of 2026 research shows data-centre waste heat could support water purification, carbon capture and district-heating-style circular uses. These applications remain technically demanding, but they signal a shift from treating AI infrastructure heat as waste to treating it as a design resource.','European Commission DG Environment; researchers; data-centre operators; municipalities; district-heating operators; sustainability teams','Opportunity','Waste-heat reuse pilots; water-positive data-centre concepts; carbon-capture integration studies; district heating feasibility checks',array['Identify opportunities','Develop solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Develop solutions: local infrastructure concepts may increasingly be screened for circular energy and water value before scaling AI-enabled facilities.','https://environment.ec.europa.eu/news/ai-data-centre-waste-heat-could-be-used-water-purification-and-carbon-capture-2026-03-30_en','Peer-reviewed article','excel-database'),
('AI-036','2026-05-29','US / EU / Global','Political','AI compliance','Public sector','Emerging issue','Act','AI procurement evidence becomes a market-access gate','NIST’s 2026 AI Agent Standards Initiative signals that secure identity, authorization, interoperability and auditability are becoming expected evidence for agentic systems. AI-specific procurement requirements are likely to move toward reusable evidence packs covering model cards, evaluation artefacts, permissions, audit logs and incident-response plans.','Public agencies; procurement teams; AI vendors; compliance officers; risk teams','Risk','RFP clauses requiring model cards; agent identity and authorization protocols; evaluation artefact requests; AI security questionnaires; audit-trail requirements',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts; Deploy solutions: procurement evidence requirements should be built into concept criteria, validation plans and launch readiness for AI-enabled offerings.','https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2026/02/announcing-ai-agent-standards-initiative-interoperable-and-secure','Standard/guideline','excel-database'),
('AI-037','2026-05-29','US / EU / Global','Political','AI content provenance','Creative industries/media','Trend','Prepare','AI content provenance moves from voluntary watermarking to compliance infrastructure','The European Commission’s 2026 Code of Practice process for marking and labelling AI-generated content is turning AI-content provenance from voluntary watermarking into operational compliance infrastructure. Providers and deployers may need machine-readable marking, detection workflows, clear labels and documented content-governance routines before transparency obligations apply.','California regulators; New York legislators; content platforms; advertisers; AI developers; creative agencies','Mixed','AI-labeling rules; code-of-practice milestones; provenance tool adoption; watermarking pilots; synthetic performer disclosures; platform policy updates',array['Create concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Deploy solutions: content provenance and disclosure assumptions should be considered when designing AI-enabled concepts and scaling market-facing content.','https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/code-practice-ai-generated-content','Regulatory document','excel-database'),
('AI-038','2026-05-29','US / Global','Environmental','AI infrastructure','Energy','Trend','Act','Dedicated energy islands become part of AI infrastructure strategy','IEA’s Energy and AI analysis shows data-centre electricity demand growing rapidly, with accelerated AI servers driving a large share of the increase and local grid integration becoming challenging because data centres concentrate power demand in specific places. Operators may respond with direct energy partnerships, flexible load arrangements and dedicated supply strategies.','Hyperscalers; utilities; energy majors; grid operators; regulators; local communities','Mixed','Data-centre electricity demand; accelerated-server power demand; grid-connection delays; direct energy partnerships; power-purchase agreements',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts; Deploy solutions: AI-enabled offerings should test energy availability, cost exposure and sustainability assumptions before scale-up.','https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-and-ai/energy-demand-from-ai','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-039','2026-05-29','US / Europe / Global','Environmental','AI energy governance','Energy','Emerging issue','Prepare','Community pushback turns AI data-centre siting into a social licence issue','IEA analysis stresses that data centres can be developed faster than energy infrastructure and are spatially concentrated, making local grid integration and siting a practical bottleneck. Community and regulator scrutiny of power, water, land use and ratepayer impacts may turn AI infrastructure into a social-licence issue for compute-intensive innovation.','Local governments; community groups; utilities; hyperscalers; energy regulators; sustainability teams','Risk','Moratoriums; grid-connection delays; utility rate cases; water-use disputes; data-centre permitting delays; local opposition',array['Identify opportunities','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Deploy solutions: resource and social-licence constraints should be screened early and reflected in scaling plans for compute-intensive AI innovation.','https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-and-ai/energy-demand-from-ai','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-040','2026-05-08','Global','Environmental','AI weather/climate','Public sector','Trend','Watch','AI weather pipelines challenge traditional forecasting infrastructure','AI weather models and end-to-end forecasting pipelines are moving from research demonstrations toward operational use. They could improve speed and access to climate intelligence, but reliability and institutional integration remain uncertain.','Weather agencies; climate researchers; AI labs; public-sector innovators; disaster-risk teams','Opportunity','Operational AI weather deployments; forecast-latency improvements; model evaluation benchmarks; public-sector pilots',array['Identify opportunities','Validate concepts']::text[],'Identify opportunities; Validate concepts: faster weather and climate intelligence can support opportunity sensing and validation for resilient products, infrastructure and services.','https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report/science','Industry report','excel-database'),
('AI-041','2026-05-29','US / Global','Social','AI companions','Consumer goods','Emerging issue','Act','AI companion safety rules turn emotional AI into a regulated product class','2026 chatbot legislation trackers show companion chatbots becoming a distinct safety and compliance concern, especially for minors, disclosures, self-harm responses and emotional or relationship-simulating systems. Emotionally engaging AI experiences may require product-safety governance closer to regulated consumer services than ordinary UX features.','Companion chatbot operators; state regulators; child-safety advocates; consumer platforms; mental-health experts','Risk','AI companion laws; chatbot-specific bills; crisis-referral protocols; minor-safety requirements; lawsuits or complaints',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts','Deploy solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts; Deploy solutions: emotionally engaging AI concepts need safety-by-design, validation of crisis protocols and deployment monitoring.','https://fpf.org/2026-chatbot-legislation-tracker/','Legal analysis','excel-database'),
('AI-042','2026-05-08','Global','Social','AI skills/workforce','Education/research','Trend','Prepare','Agent orchestration becomes a core AI workforce capability','As organisations deploy agents across workflows, workers increasingly need to supervise, evaluate and orchestrate AI systems rather than only use single copilots. This shifts capability-building toward judgement, delegation, verification and governance skills.','Employers; training providers; cloud vendors; HR leaders; innovation teams; universities','Opportunity','AI fluency programmes; agent-orchestration training; job redesign metrics; internal agent-builder communities',array['Create concepts','Validate concepts','Develop solutions']::text[],'Create concepts; Validate concepts; Develop solutions: workforce capability-building should support human-agent collaboration from concept design through solution development.','https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/google_cloud_ai_agent_trends_2026_report.pdf','Industry report','excel-database'),
